---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Felix Geelhaar"
  description="R&D ops leader and open-source author. Writes on platform topology and engineering effectiveness."
  nav="home"
>
  <section class="page-header" style="border-bottom: none;">
    <h1>Platforms rot from the middle.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Three weeks of operating-model debt look identical to a year of it &mdash; until they don't.
      I work on the middle layer where decision rights blur, ownership erodes, and platform
      debt compounds. Treat it like a product, not a process.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What's here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}writing`}>Writing</a> &mdash; long-form essays on platform topology, error-budget discipline, and the operating models that hold modern R&amp;D together.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}lab`}>Lab</a> &mdash; open-source projects. Small on purpose.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}talks`}>Talks</a> &mdash; conference talks and recordings when the room is right.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}work`}>Work</a> &mdash; engagement shapes if you want me on the problem.</li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}about`}>About</a> &mdash; the long version of the bio.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Right now</h2>
    <p>
      Focused on the connective tissue between strategy, platform, and product so engineering teams ship
      clearly and senior engineers stay senior. See <a href={`${BASE}now`}>/now</a> for the current quarter.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
